{
  "$comment": "Validator config, not a token file, the design system itself is the CSS. Each pair is a foreground var that must stay legible on a background var, at a WCAG 2 ratio, in the listed modes. scripts/lint.mjs checks the shipped public palettes. min: 4.5 = AA normal text, 3 = non-text/large. This set is deliberately BROAD: every text token must clear AA on every everyday content surface (canvas / surface / surface-raised / surface-sunken) so a designer can pair any text with any surface without checking. `bg-well` is excluded on purpose (it is a void a surface sits in front of, not a surface content sits on), and cross-status pairs (danger text on success-subtle) are excluded as nonsensical. Disabled + decorative pairs are absent per WCAG 1.4.3 / 1.4.11.",
